From ef4f6e4cba7d6b62c3956832671794cd3b6b1fac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 16:03:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] docs(retrieval-server): describe the Typst-only PDF
 renderer

development.md now covers the state after the xhtml2pdf removal: local
setup without the x2p constraints, one-shot render children and their env
vars, and the renderer section (PDF_RENDERER only, the obsolete canary and
script-route variables, x2p_v1-pinned runs rendering with Typst); the
letterhead section no longer says x2p_v1 ignores it. The Dockerfile's
comments, the graph_tools README's dependency column, the fonts README and
the fonts_cover and fetch_fonts docstrings no longer describe xhtml2pdf or
the script route.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01R4WFJ4gcPzabKrzbRdXcQF
